\section{Layers}{

ndopred keeps apart what is calculated, what is evidenced, what is
proposed and what is approved:
\itemize{
\item \code{input} and \code{run}: what the run was given, and its settings;
\item \code{calculated}: measured from the records (EOO, AOO, counts);
\item \code{indication}: derived from the records, but not evidence (clusters,
raw changes, trend estimates);
\item \code{parameter}: values the criteria need besides the records
(generation length);
\item \code{evidence}: entered by an assessor in the evidence file;
\item \code{proposal}: the engine's proposal and what it rests on;
\item \code{approved}: the final category and its state, set by the group experts;
\item \code{diagnostic}: the reason for every empty value (\verb{issue_*}).
}
